  "liner": {
   "body_md": "Mountain Goats performed at the Festival For The Eno in Durham, North Carolina, on Saturday, July 6, 2013 [1]. The recording, captured by Dan Schram, runs for 52 minutes and 17 seconds [1]. The uploader dedicated the tape to the memory of Landon Korabek [1]. This is the only available recording of the show [1]. The setlist includes sixteen songs, starting with “High Hawk Season” and “Love Love Love” [1]. Rare tracks such as “Absolute Lithops Effect,” “For Charles Bronson,” “Ripple,” and “Rotten Stinking Mouthpiece” appear in the set [1]. The band also played “Dinu Lapatti's Bones,” “Broom People,” “Jenny,” “Dance Music,” and “You Were Cool” [1]. Later songs include “Woke Up New,” “International Small Arms Traffic Blues,” and “Surrounded” [1]. The performance concludes with “Alpha Rats Nest” and “No Children” [1]. Listener reviews for this specific recording describe the music as featuring man, guitar, and songs about death and summer [3]. One reviewer noted the high-quality banter, highlighting an interaction where an MC commented on a song the audience knew the chorus to [4]. Another simply stated that no further explanation was needed [2]. The recording is rated five stars by three listeners [1].",
